@format 1
@id media-loading.common.files-selection
@title Files selection
@section Media loading
@area Common
@entry row-press, row-release, select-all, remove-selected, clear-files
@summary Trace shared Files interactions that publish a current path, including the two-stage selection behavior of direct Remove.
@related media-loading.common.files-clear, media-loading.common.docket-removal, media-loading.in-split-tab, media-loading.in-edit-tab, media-loading.in-convert-tab, media-loading.in-audio-tab, media-loading.in-merge-tab, media-loading.in-funnel-tab
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag common
@tag selection

@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList
@alias docket = Cadroue.Application.LDocket

[row-press] Files row mouse press <input>
- Apply normal, Control, or Shift selection for the pressed row @ list.PListPressHandle(...)
> row-press-publish

[row-release] Files row mouse release <input>
- Release a captured row interaction and collapse a retained multi-selection only when a collapse path is pending @ list.PListReleaseHandle(...)
> row-release-result

[select-all] Files Control+A <input>
- Test Control+A against the current Files selection and docket contents @ list.PListKeyHandle(...)
> select-all-result

[remove-selected] Remove selected Files <input>
- Resolve selected unlocked paths and remember the first removed index before performing synchronous docket removal @ list.PListRemove(...)
> remove-result

[clear-files] Remove all Files button <input>
- Invoke the registered Remove All callback and enter PListClear @ list.PListButtonBuild(...)
> map:media-loading.common.files-clear

[row-press-publish] Press selection publication <process>
- Publish the selected current path as part of the row-selection operation @ list.PListCurrentApply(...)
> row-press-output

[row-release-result] Release outcome <decision>
- Republish the collapsed row only when the earlier press left a collapse path pending @ list.PListReleaseHandle(...)
? "Selection collapsed" > row-release-publish
? "No collapse pending" > row-release-nochange

[select-all-result] Select-all eligibility <decision>
- Apply the full selection only when Control+A, an existing selection, and at least one docket path are present @ list.PListKeyHandle(...)
  @ list.PListSelectionApply(...)
? "Eligible" > select-all-publish
? "Ineligible" > select-all-nochange

[remove-result] Remove eligibility <decision>
- Continue only when at least one selected path is unlocked and removable @ list.PListRemove(...)
? "Removal performed" > remove-docket-call
? "Nothing removable" > remove-nochange

[row-press-output] Current path after press <output>
= The scenario-specific selected-path adapter receives the published path.

[row-release-publish] Release selection publication <process>
- Publish the collapsed current path @ list.PListCurrentApply(...)
> row-release-output

[row-release-nochange] Release changes nothing <output>
= No current-path publication occurs.

[select-all-publish] Select-all current publication <process>
- Preserve the current path when possible, otherwise publish the last selected path @ list.PListCurrentApply(...)
> select-all-output

[select-all-nochange] Select All ignored <output>
= No current-path publication occurs.

[remove-docket-call] Synchronous docket-removal subflow <process>
- Call LDocketPathsRemove from PListRemove; the complete Common / Docket removal sequence runs synchronously before this call returns, including any first-remaining PListPathChange and PListClearChange viewer cleanup @ list.PListRemove(...)
  @ docket.LDocketPathsRemove(...)
! The common Docket removal map is a call-return subflow here, not the end of PListRemove.
> remove-final-select

[remove-nochange] Removal ignored <output>
= The Files current path is unchanged.

[row-release-output] Current path after release <output>
= The scenario-specific selected-path adapter receives the republished path.

[select-all-output] Current path after Select All <output>
= The scenario-specific selected-path adapter receives the published path.

[remove-final-select] Direct Remove resumes and selects again <process>
- After LDocketPathsRemove returns, reread remaining paths and call PListSelectApply with null or the clamped original index; this synchronously publishes PListPathChange again @ list.PListRemove(...)
  @ list.PListSelectApply(...)
  @ list.PListCurrentApply(...)
! This second publication occurs after any forced viewer close performed by PListClearChange, so it can start a fresh request and supersede an earlier replacement request from PListDocketRemoveHandle.
> remove-output

[remove-output] Current path after direct Remove <output>
= PListRemove has finished its second selection publication; an empty docket publishes null and media-tab adapters ignore it.
